  "notes": [
    "MANUAL run, not a CI measurement: the real profiles are periodic/manual only. Kept as a reference point for what a real L2 comparison of a modest real C++ library costs.",
    "CAVEAT: the two revisions' public header trees digest IDENTICALLY (PR #216 is a CI-only change), so this is in practice an EQUIVALENCE comparison -- same headers, two builds -- not a header-changing temporal one. A temporal PVXS number needs a revision pair that actually changes a public header.",
    "The ~10x spread between the two libraries is the size of their public header surfaces (client.h+data.h+server.h vs. one iochooks.h).",
    "sampled_peak_tree_bytes is a sampled lower bound on concurrent process-tree RSS at a 0.05s interval, not an exact peak; ru_maxrss_bytes is the separate per-process kernel high-water mark and is shared across both rows because it is cumulative over the measuring process's reaped children.",
    "EPICS base and both pvxs revisions were built as SETUP, outside every measured window. Preparation also needed libevent-dev, which EPICS base does not require but pvxs does.",
    "Reproduce: scripts/l2_real_profiles.py's prepare_script(PVXS), then a compare per library with per-side labelled include roots (--include old:ctxN=... / new:ctxN=...). Note that mixing a labelled side-scoped include with unlabelled global ones did NOT apply the global roots; every root must be given per side."
